{
  "key": "electric-substation",
  "name": "Transmission Substation (IEC 61850)",
  "category": "OT",
  "description": "A 138/13.8 kV IEC 61850 substation seen from the station SPAN. Station bus: an SEL-3530 RTAC gateway polling multi-vendor protection IEDs (SEL-451/751, ABB REF615, GE Multilin 850, Siemens SIPROTEC 5 7SJ85) over MMS and DNP3, protection GOOSE between the feeder IEDs, an SEL-2488 PTP grandmaster (IEC 61850-9-3 over Ethernet) and a local HMI / engineering laptop doing SEL relay-settings sessions. Process bus: SEL-401 and SIPROTEC 6MU85 merging units streaming 9-2LE sampled values to the SEL-487E transformer differential, timed by the boundary-clock switch. The control centre (SCADA over DNP3, backup over IEC 104, NMS) and the corporate office sit across the utility WAN (wan_rtt_ms). Planted findings: GOOSE from an unexpected publisher (a test set left on the bus), relay engineering straight from the corporate office, a rogue PTP grandmaster, factory SEL passwords in cleartext. Run: tgt run --env electric-substation --pcap sub.pcap --once --rate 0",
